morbius may be a solo movie for the  marvel anti-hero but it references at  least five other villains from  spider-man's rogues gallery did you  catch them all these are the small  details you missed in morbius  let's get this out of the way morbius is  not in the marvel cinematic universe and  it's not produced by marvel studios it's  a sony product part of its own universe  of marvel characters namely most of the  marvel comics characters mainly  associated with spider-man there's only  three movies in this universe the two  venom movies and now morbius but that  doesn't mean more movies in sony's own  series aren't on the way an early  conversation between nichols and milo  sees the wealthy villain explain that he  recently crossed paths with a certain  russian gentleman which is why he's  hired bodyguards to look after him he  doesn't go into more detail but it seems  likely that this mysterious russian he's  referring to is actually craven the  hunter sure there have been a few  different russian villains to grace the  pages of the spider-man comics over the  years but considering sony is working on  a craven the hunter movie it seems  likely that this is a reference to the  iconic hunter craven's real name is  sergey kravinov and he's been a  long-standing spider-man villain first  going up against the wall crawler back  in 1964's amazing spider-man issue  number 15. craven has gone after the  spider for decades and he even dons the  costume himself in the iconic story line  craven's last hunt to prove that he can  best the hero by being a better  vigilante than him the craven the hunter  movie started production in london in  march 2022 as fans spotted aaron taylor  johnson filming a car chase through the  streets the film is currently slated for  a january 13th 2023 release so it'll be  quite some time before fans get an  official look at the spin-off movie  however it's likely he'll be a morally  ambiguous anti-hero rather than a  full-blown bad guy  one of the key locations in the film is  horizon labs where morbius looks after  children with the same blood disorder  that he has while also carrying out his  research into curing the condition this  isn't just a random name horizon labs  has been a huge part of the spider-man  comics in the last decade as peter  parker worked there during dan's slot's  run on the character it's a place for  gifted scientists to work on the most  cutting edge technology and ideas  without the restraints of having to  pitch them to a board of directors  morbius also works for horizon in the  comics and he is the one who creates a  serum that saves everyone in new york  when the events of spider island turn  everyone into giant arachnids but he's  not the only villain to grace the  laboratory's halls otto octavius aka dr  octopus also works for the company after  he transfers his consciousness into  peter's brain in amazing spider-man  issue number 700 and he uses horizon as  a way of developing new technology for  his own heroic career it's also worth  pointing out that horizon also has a  floating laboratory on a boat called the  zenith so they can also operate in  international waters but it's got a  different name in morbius  a key sequence in the film sees morbius  undergo his experimental procedure with  the help of his love interest  colleague martine bancroft on a huge  ship way off the coast of long island  this is because the procedure isn't  approved by the united states food and  drug association so they won't be  prosecuted just for carrying it out it  all goes south when morbius transforms  into a blood-sucking monster and  slaughters the gang of mercenaries that  they've hired to protect them  awkward  but the ship itself is called the myrnow  a neat reference to the famed director f  w murnow who helmed the first ever  vampire movie 1922's nosferatu the  german silent film is an unofficial  adaptation of graham stoker's dracula  and follows similar story beats to the  original tale including scenes where  count orlock kills the crew of a ship as  he travels from transylvania to germany  although morbius is far from a  traditional vampire story with the main  character explicitly being a living  vampire it's nice to see an homage to  the very first cinematic bloodsucker in  this unorthodox modern day take  just in case it isn't clear that morbius  takes place in the same universe as the  hugely successful venom franchise the  film spells it out for the audience a  couple of times over the course of  morbius's adventure when the authorities  first find the murnau with a horde of  bled-out bodies on board fbi agent  rodriguez notes to agent stroud that  they haven't had a weird case like this  since oh  around fall 2018  we haven't had anything this good since  that thing in san francisco  it's an obvious reference to eddie brock  and venom demonstrating that the  symbiotic anti-hero isn't exactly a  secret on the streets the lethal  protector got into even more trouble in  the 2021 sequel let there be carnage  when he went up against the twisted  cletus cassidy and when morbius takes  over an underground lab used by a  counterfeit gang he jokingly intimidates  one of them by making a reference to the  lethal protector  i  am  this means that news about venom has  spread across the country although it's  not quite clear what the public knows  about the symbiote other than the fact  that he occasionally eats criminals and  fights other alien goo monsters in san  francisco it's also not clear why  michael morbius knows venom's cool line  either maybe you saw the movie  we  are them  it'll be interesting to see whether  venom and morbius will ever share the  screen together but sony seems dead set  on delivering a sinister six team-up  movie at some point venom isn't usually  a member of that team at least not in  the comics but it's still a possibility  that they might team up on screen  sony might not have the rights to the  character but morbius writers matt sasma  and burke sharpless managed to squeeze a  hulk reference into the movie  nonetheless although morbius's  transformation cures him of his blood  disorder and grants him enhanced speed  and strength as well as unique  echolocation ability it also means that  he has to feed on blood so that he  doesn't revert back to his sickly self  he manages to sustain himself on  artificial blood for a little while but  it just doesn't last as long as the real  thing and when morbius finds himself  wrongfully locked up in the manhattan  detention facility for the murder of a  nurse in horizon labs he starts to get a  little angry he makes it clear to  rodriguez and shroud how desperate he is  for blood saying you won't like me when  i'm hungry while he doesn't say these  days the line is a definite callback to  the incredible hulk tv series from the  1970s starring bill bixby as dr david  bruce banner and lou ferrigno as the  titular green monster  don't make me angry  you wouldn't like me when i'm angry  it effectively became banner's  catchphrase so much so that the actual  mcu has been going out of its way not to  say it that said the mcu does have its  own version of the iconic line with  bruce revealing in the avengers  i'm always angry  just to reassure fans that this movie is  indeed spider-man related the daily  bugle newspaper shows up throughout the  film and its headlines are often easter  eggs the first one makes a reference to  a rhino getting loose from a zoo this  doesn't exactly confirm that the famous  spider-man villain necessarily shares a  universe with morbius since the headline  sounds like it involves a literal rhino  rather than the super supervillain of  the same name it's still a cute  reference the rhino is another of  spider-man's more famous villains in the  comics arguably more well-known than  morbius himself he's known for his brute  strength and the fact that he dresses up  in a rhino costume the rhino previously  smashed his way into live action in the  amazing spider-man 2 where he was played  by paul giamatti he probably would have  played a part in the original sinister  six movie that sony was developing with  drew goddard before sony reset its  spider-man plans after the movie  underperformed  the second reference on the daily  bugle's front page reads black cat  friend or foe which seemingly confirms  that felicia hardy exists here too the  character previously appeared in the  amazing spider-man 2 played by rogue one  star felicity jones in a minor role she  briefly shows up as one of the  assistants working at ozcorp before  harry osborne notices her and hires her  as his personal assistant she was also  presumably going to have a larger role  in that universe before sony scrapped  the third installment of the amazing  spider-man black cat is an iconic  character in the spider-man mythos  largely because she's one of the  webslinger's frequent love interests the  burglar first appears in 1979's amazing  spider-man issue number 194 when she  hatches a plan to break her dying father  out of prison it also establishes that  anyone who crosses her falls foul of her  bad luck riffing off the common  superstition regarding actual black cats  it's highly likely that black cat will  show up in a future film with sony  already having at least one movie for  the character in development the studio  was originally planning to use the femme  fatale alongside mercenary silver sable  in a team-up adventure titled silver and  black from director gina prince bythwood  the movie was set aside and the director  moved on to other projects however the  filmmaker told looper in 2020 that she'd  love to return to the characters with  the script she wrote  but wait there's a third daily bugle  headline referencing yet another member  of spidey's rogues gallery chameleon's  great escape suggests that demetrius  mirdanikov has already had a brush with  the authorities and has even managed to  escape prison if it's on the front page  of the bugle although many of the  webslinger's villains take inspiration  from animals chameleon doesn't actually  dress up like the reptile he's named  after instead he's a master of disguise  and can impersonate anyone he likes to  carry up robberies and assassinations  surprisingly fans might have already  seen a version of chameleon in live  action with a dimitri showing up in  spider-man far from home as one of nick  fury's associates  that  is dmitry  he's played by newman a car in the mcu  but he doesn't actually get to do  anything comparable to his comic book  origins chameleon first shows up in  1962's amazing spider-man issue number  one where he steals highly classified  missile plans and frames the titular  hero for the crime the white mask  wearing villain will next be seen in the  craven the hunter solo movie this time  played by fred heshinger it's worth  pointing out that chameleon is actually  craven's half-brother so hopefully that  dynamic gets the spotlight in the 2023  movie  it just wouldn't be a comic book movie  if the big bad didn't go after the  hero's love interest in the dramatic  finale and morbius is no exception  unfortunately milo catches martine  bancroft and forces her to cry out for  her moody vampire bow in a bid to kick  start the predictable final battle a  hero and a villain with the same set of  superpowers  groundbreaking anyway he ultimately  leaves martine bleeding out on a rooftop  for morbius to find her in a generous  act of sacrifice she lets the good  doctor drink her blood so he's fully  powered to kill milo but before she dies  a drop of morbius's own blood drips into  her mouth and she licks her teeth with  it weird but hey she's dying so he won't  judge one of the final moments of the  film sees martine wake up with bright  red eyes implying that she's returned as  a vampire this could be picked up in a  morbius sequel and there's a precedent  for it in the 30th issue of the comic  book fear in which martine is turned  into a vampire by an enemy of morbius  although she becomes a living vampire  like morbius her newfound abilities make  her aspire to be a true vampire like  dracula  oh dear  hello martine vancroft and bring on  morbius 2.  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite movies and tv shows are  coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one

